title: A toggles list
intro: A Toggles List makes an on/off switch for each row of a table, remembered by the game and starting as the table says.

project: Empty | Toggles List

chapter: A table of fires | Data > New Table
menu: Data > New Table...
prompt: Fires
click: tables:header:Value
click: tables:column:name
key: Ctrl+A
type: On\n
columntype: On = yes/no
cell: Row 1 > Name = Rain
cell: Rain > On = yes
click: tables:addrow
cell: Row 2 > Name = Smoke
cell: Smoke > On = no
expecttable: 2 rows, 1 column
say: A table of fires: the events that slow the game down, with a column for whether each starts on.

chapter: A switch for each row | Toggles List
create: Panel
rename: Options
set: Panel.Open = true
add: TogglesList
explain: field:TogglesList.Table | Table | A Toggles List makes a switch for each row of this table. Adding it brought a Layout, which lines the rows up.
set: TogglesList.Table = Fires
explain: field:TogglesList.DefaultColumn | Default Column | The yes or no column says whether each row starts on, until the player flips it.
set: TogglesList.DefaultColumn = On
explain: field:TogglesList.SaveAs | Save As | Each switch is remembered in the save data under this name, where {row} is the row's name: fire.Rain, fire.Smoke. Scripts read them with GetBool, like any Toggle.
set: TogglesList.SaveAs = fire.{row}

chapter: Play | Flip Smoke on
play
wait: 1
expectvalue: Rain/Switch.Toggle.IsOn = true
expectvalue: Smoke/Switch.Toggle.IsOn = false
say: Rain starts on and Smoke off, as the table says.
gameclick: Smoke/Switch
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Smoke/Switch.Toggle.IsOn = true
say: Flipping Smoke is remembered under fire.Smoke, so next time the game starts it is on.
stop
